d map (2/3), system picks randomly from {studied, unstudied} -> 1/2 chance\n            // So probability = (2/3) * (1/2) = 1/3\n            \n            // For case2 (2 studied, 1 unstudied shown):\n            // Johnny will discard the unstudied map\n            // Opponent discards randomly:\n            // - If opponent discards studied map (2/3), system picks randomly from {studied, unstudied} -> 1/2 chance\n            // - If opponent discards unstudied map (1/3), system picks randomly from 2 studied maps -> 1 chance\n            // So probability = (2/3)*(1/2) + (1/3)*1 = 1/3 + 1/3 = 2/3\n            \n            // For case3 (3 studied shown):\n            // Johnny will discard one studied map\n            // Opponent discards randomly:\n            // - System picks randomly from remaining 2 studied maps -> 1 chance\n            // So probability = 1\n            \n            double prob = 0.0;\n            if (total > 0) {\n                prob = (double)favorable / total;\n                \n                // Weighted probability based on cases\n                double case1Prob = (n-i >= 2) ? ((double)(i * (n-i) * (n-i-1) / 2) / total) : 0;\n                double case2Prob = (i >= 2 && n-i >= 1) ? ((double)(i * (i-1) / 2 * (n-i)) / total) : 0;\n                double case3Prob = (i >= 3) ? ((double)(i * (i-1) * (i-2) / 6) / total) : 0;\n                \n                prob = case1Prob * (1.0/3.0) + case2Prob * (2.0/3.0) + case3Prob * 1.0;\n            }\n            \n            if (prob >= p - 1e-8) {\n                pw.println(i);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        pw.flush();\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.4185804502631072e-05, -8.583032467868179e-06, 0.0, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, -1.8954096958623268e-05, -1.07287787614041e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0028076060